# English Documentation Rule

## Code Comments
All code comments, JSDoc, and inline documentation must be written in English.

### Examples:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct - English comment
// This function handles user authentication

// ❌ Incorrect - French comment  
// Cette fonction gère l'authentification utilisateur
```

## README Documentation
All README.md files and documentation must be written in English.

### Examples:
```markdown
<!-- ✅ Correct - English documentation -->
# Component Overview
This component provides...

<!-- ❌ Incorrect - French documentation -->
# Vue d'ensemble du composant
Ce composant fournit...
```

## Linear Tickets
All Linear ticket descriptions, comments, and updates must be written in English.

### Examples:
```markdown
<!-- ✅ Correct - English ticket -->
## Implementation Details
- Feature: Add user authentication
- Status: In Progress

<!-- ❌ Incorrect - French ticket -->
## Détails d'implémentation
- Fonctionnalité: Ajouter l'authentification utilisateur
- Statut: En cours
```

## TypeScript Interfaces and Types
All interface documentation, property descriptions, and type comments must be in English.

### Examples:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct - English interface documentation
export interface UserConfig {
  /** User's email address */
  email: string;
  /** Whether notifications are enabled */
  notificationsEnabled: boolean;
}

// ❌ Incorrect - French interface documentation
export interface UserConfig {
  /** Adresse email de l'utilisateur */
  email: string;
  /** Si les notifications sont activées */
  notificationsEnabled: boolean;
}
```

## Exception
The only exception is for user-facing strings that are displayed to end users, which should be in French as per the project requirements. These are typically found in translation files or UI text.

### Examples:
```typescript
// ✅ Correct - French user-facing strings
const messages = {
  welcome: "Bienvenue",
  login: "Se connecter"
}

// ✅ Correct - English code comments
// Handle user login process
const handleLogin = () => {
  // Implementation here
}
```

## Enforcement
- All new code must follow this rule
- When reviewing code, ensure comments and documentation are in English
- Update existing French comments to English when modifying files
- Use English for all technical documentation and API descriptions